infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title The boundary, not the tool: god package vs split by domain
  desc Same Turborepo, same remote cache — only the package boundaries change
  compares
    - label God shared / utils package
      children
        - label Cache hit rate 4 percent
          desc One line in shared re-hashes every task in the graph
        - label Median PR CI 38 minutes
          desc Even a typo in docs runs the full build
        - label Changes in 70 percent of PRs
          desc A grab-bag name cannot say no to a new export
        - label Sits under all 6 builds
          desc Its output hash feeds every dependent cache key
    - label Split by domain and change frequency
      children
        - label Cache hit rate 85 percent
          desc Stable leaves separated from hot domain logic
        - label Median PR CI 6 minutes
          desc Only the changed subgraph actually executes
        - label A billing change rebuilds 2 nodes
          desc Invalidation stops at the real dependents
        - label Affected-only with --filter
          desc CI ignores tasks outside the blast radius
